positive ninhydrin test","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baf"},{"id":"qz_69de4f822ee0e063d9292f01","_quizrrId":"69de4f822ee0e063d9292f01","q":"Maltose on treatment with dilute $HCl$ gives:","options":["D-Glucose","D-Fructose","D-Galactose","D-Glucose and D-Fructose"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-46d22fef9984fc7c.png?alt=media&v=qxmd265\" style=\"width: 500px; height:auto;max-width:100%;display:block;background:#fff;\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-46d22fef9984fc7c.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-46d22fef9984fc7c.png?alt=media&v=qxmd265\" onerror=\"if(window.QxOwnedFigs&&QxOwnedFigs.retryOnError)QxOwnedFigs.retryOnError(this)\" class=\"qx-pool-fig qx-no-wm qx-sol-fig\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"eager\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Maltose is a disaccharide which contain D-glucose as a monosaccharide. Thus, Hydrolysis of maltose& with $dilHCl$ gives D-& glucose.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baf"},{"id":"qz_69de4f822ee0e063d9292f06","_quizrrId":"69de4f822ee0e063d9292f06","q":"<p>Match List-I with List-II.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">List-I<br /> Natural Amino& <br /> acid</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">List-II<br /> One Letter& <br /> Code</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(A)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Arginine</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(I)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$D$</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(B)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Aspartic acid</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(II)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$N$</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(C)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Asparagine</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(III)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$A$</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(D)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Alanine</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(IV)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$R$</td> </tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>","options":["(A)−IV, B−I, (C)−II, (D)−III","(A)−I, B−III, (C)−IV, (D)−II","(A)−III, B−I, (C)−II, (D)−IV","(A)−IV, B−I, (C)−III, (D)−II"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<blockquote><p>The single letter amino acid codes is fairly easy to remember. In eleven cases out of twenty,& it is just the first letter.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Natural Amino acid</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">One Letter Code</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(A)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Arginine</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(IV)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$R$</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(B)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Aspartic acid</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(I)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$D$</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(C)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Asparagine</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(II)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$N$</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(D)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Alanine</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">(III)</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$A$</td> </tr>\t</tbody></table></blockquote>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baf"},{"id":"qz_69de4f822ee0e063d9292f0b","_quizrrId":"69de4f822ee0e063d9292f0b","q":"The $\\alpha$-Helix and $\\beta$ - Pleated sheet structures of protein are associated with its :","options":["tertiary structure","quaternary structure","secondary structure","primary structure"],"answer":2,"answers":[2],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"$\\alpha$-helix and $\\beta$-pleated sheet belongs to secondary structure of protein, which have hydrogen bonds.","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baf"},{"id":"qz_69de4f822ee0e063d9292f10","_quizrrId":"69de4f822ee0e063d9292f10","q":"Identify the incorrect statement from the following.","options":["Amylose is a branched chain polymer of glucose","Starch is a polymer of $\\alpha - D$ glucose","$\\beta -$Glycosidic linkage makes cellulose polymer","Glycogen is called as animal starch"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"Amylose is linear chain polymer of& $\\alpha - D - Glucose$& whereas amylopectin is branched chain polymer of same compound. Other statements are correct. ","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baf"},{"id":"qz_69de4f822ee0e063d9292f15","_quizrrId":"69de4f822ee0e063d9292f15","q":"The correct structure of histidine in a strongly acidic solution $\\left(pH = 2\\right)$ is","options":["<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fjee